# London boroughs: a conformant map of population density, Census 2021.
#
# Values: usual residents per square kilometre, Census 2021 table TS006
#   (Population density), 33 London local authorities. Office for National
#   Statistics, released 2 November 2022, via Nomis (dataset NM_2026_1).
#   https://www.nomisweb.co.uk/datasets/c2021ts006
# Zones: Local Authority Districts (December 2024) Boundaries UK BFE, ONS
#   Open Geography Portal. https://geoportal.statistics.gov.uk/
# River: River Thames centreline from OS Open Rivers (Ordnance Survey,
#   2026 edition). https://osdatahub.os.uk/downloads/open/OpenRivers
#
# Source: Office for National Statistics licensed under the Open
# Government Licence v3.0. Contains OS data (c) Crown copyright and
# database right 2024-2026. Licence: https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/
#   doc/open-government-licence/version/3/
#
# Simplified: boundaries are the full-extent (to mid-river) versions,
# simplified together (shapely coverage_simplify, 250 m) so neighbours
# keep shared edges; islets under 0.05 sq km are left out. The Thames is
# the network route from Staines to Purfleet, simplified to 60 m.
# Coordinates are British National Grid kilometres: down from northing
# 202 km, across from easting 502.5 km; 0.2 inch per km.
# Zone order and values follow ONS codes E09000001 (City of London)
# to E09000033 (Westminster).
